data: {"messages":[{"content":"<uploaded_files>\nThe following files were uploaded in this message:\n\n- Trafic.mp4 (72.4 MB)\n  Path: /mnt/user-data/uploads/Trafic.mp4\n\nYou can read these files using the `read_file` tool with the paths shown above.\n</uploaded_files>\n\n检测这段视频里的行人、轿车、公交车和卡车，输出每帧的位置框、类别和置信度。","additional_kwargs":{"files":[{"filename":"Trafic.mp4","size":75965424,"path":"/mnt/user-data/uploads/Trafic.mp4","status":"uploaded"}]},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"b5d1e8e5-9c98-4b90-8c17-19be4e0696d1"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze-video</name>\n      <description>专业视频抽帧与取证准备技能。支持场景检测、多阶段帧提取和 metadata 生成，供 single-video-event-analysis 做 LLM 审帧使用；本 skill 不再作为最终事件检测入口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/analyze-video/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>batch-video-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Batch ingest local monitoring videos into the Elasticsearch video library after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, with metadata, sampled-frame object summaries, and searchable documents. For direct user video ingestion, ingest-and-embed, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, or business video-library requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear ingestion plan, video directory, video manifest, camera_id, or multiple video files to index for later retrieval and statistics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/batch-video-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>camera-health-check</name>\n      <description>Check video monitoring camera quality from sampled frames and return health status before downstream event generation. Use when Codex has camera_id and frames and needs to gate or downgrade event confidence for offline, unavailable, degraded, black-screen, blurred, occluded, frozen, corrupted, or shifted camera feeds.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/camera-health-check/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>city-video-intelligence</name>\n      <description>Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>duplicate-event-merge</name>\n      <description>Merge duplicate video event candidates from the same camera, event type, ROI, evidence frames, or overlapping time window. Use after single-video-event-analysis or batch video analysis when Codex has a list of Event Candidate records and needs canonical events plus duplicate mappings.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/duplicate-event-merge/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-package-generation</name>\n      <description>Generate an evidence package manifest for indexed monitoring videos or event/search results, including snapshot evidence and optional short video clips. Use when Codex needs a package_id, manifest URI, evidence items, hashes, and reusable evidence artifacts.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-package-generation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-snapshot</name>\n      <description>Generate snapshot evidence for video monitoring event candidates. Use when Codex has an event, event_id, evidence_frame_ids, image_uri, or frame list and needs a snapshot URI, SHA-256 integrity hash, created_at timestamp, privacy masking status, and Evidence schema output.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-snapshot/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>ffmpeg-utils</name>\n      <description>视频处理工具集，支持视频截取和关键帧提取。常用于将监控视频剪辑为证据片段。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/ffmpeg-utils/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>frame-sampling</name>\n      <description>Sample structured frames from an existing video file. Use when Codex has video_path, file_path, raw_segment_uri, camera_id, sampling_strategy, capture_seconds, or provided frame records and needs stable Frame schema outputs. This skill exposes OpenCV-backed real video frame extraction.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/frame-sampling/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>human-review-routing</name>\n      <description>Decide whether video monitoring event candidates require manual review. Use after event generation and evidence creation when Codex has event confidence, event_type, review_threshold, camera_health, high_risk_event_types, newly added camera signals, or enforcement-impact flags and needs review queue routing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-detection</name>\n      <description>Detect visible objects in sampled video frames and return standard Detection schema only. Use when Codex needs YOLO labels, confidences, and bounding boxes for people, vehicles, or COCO objects. Do not use this skill to infer events, abnormal behavior, accidents, fights, falls, congestion, intrusion, smoke/fire, or business semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-detection/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-statistics</name>\n      <description>Compute object statistics for monitoring videos from Elasticsearch video-library records or local detections/tracks JSON. Use when Codex needs counts by label, camera, time bucket, or movement state.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-statistics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-tracking</name>\n      <description>Track detected objects across video frames and return Track schema for object analytics only. Use when Codex has frame-level detections and needs stable track ids, trajectories, duration, last bbox, movement state, confidence, and evidence frame ids. Do not use this skill to infer video events or abnormal behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-tracking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>privacy-masking</name>\n      <description>Mask sensitive visual data in video evidence such as faces, license plates, phone numbers, and doorplates. Use when Codex has an evidence image URI and explicit sensitive_regions bbox coordinates, or privacy_masking config and needs a masked URI before exposing snapshots or clips externally. This skill exposes OpenCV image read/write and Gaussian blur masking for real files.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/privacy-masking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>roi-mapping</name>\n      <description>Match detections or tracks against configured camera ROI polygons for geometric object analytics. Use when Codex has camera_id plus tracks or objects and needs point containment or bbox overlap matches for configured areas. Do not use this skill to decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/roi-mapping/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>single-video-event-analysis</name>\n      <description>Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-embedding-index</name>\n      <description>Generate text embeddings or StreetModel sampled-frame image embeddings for video-library documents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request. Only enrich citybrain-video-library in place. For direct user StreetModel, ingest-and-embed, semantic retrieval, benchmark, or keyword-vs-vector requests, load city-video-intelligence first.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-embedding-index/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-object-analytics</name>\n      <description>Deterministic structured entrypoint for local-video object detection and cross-frame tracking. Use for direct requests to count visible people, vehicles, or other objects, or to track them across frames. The dedicated video_object_analytics tool owns all CLI parameters, model configuration, persistent paths, and downstream skill order.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-object-analytics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-search</name>\n      <description>Search indexed monitoring videos from text, images, structured filters, or precomputed vectors. Use for keyword retrieval, LLM-optimized text-to-video semantic retrieval, combined keyword/vector search, or image-to-video similarity search against StreetModel/Qwen3-VL video vectors.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-segment-extraction</name>\n      <description>Extract playable short video evidence clips around event times. Use when Codex has event_id, camera_id, raw_segment_uri, event_time, event_elapsed_seconds, pre_seconds, or post_seconds and needs an MP4 clip URI plus clip time range. This skill exposes FFmpeg-backed clipping for real local videos and memory-backed synthetic clips for tests.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-segment-extraction/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-stream-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Normalize an existing local video file after city-video-intelligence has routed a video-library or analysis request, returning raw segment/session metadata such as duration, resolution, frame rate, codec, and session times. Use it for any \"read this video's duration / resolution / fps / codec / metadata\" or \"turn this video into a standard analysis input\" request instead of running ffprobe by hand. For direct user ingestion, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, search, statistics, evidence, or camera-health requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear plan and a local MP4/MOV/AVI/MKV file before frame sampling.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-stream-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"fe6654c5-46eb-4e9c-9d77-3b04a014fc08"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 检测这段视频里的行人、轿车、公交车和卡车，输出每帧的位置框、类别和置信度。\n任务规划：\n1. 调用视频解析组件读取输入源，完成视频流解码与逐帧抽帧处理，核对分辨率与编码格式以适配后续视觉模型，产出标准化帧序列及基础元数据。\n2. 基于视频监控场景的多目标检测能力，将抽帧序列依次输入识别引擎，针对行人、轿车、公交车和卡车执行推理计算，并应用预设置信度阈值过滤低质量预测，产出逐帧原始检测结果集。\n3. 对原始检测结果进行坐标空间转换与时序逻辑校验，依据连续帧间目标运动规律剔除异常跳变框与重叠冗余框，统一数据输出口径，产出结构化且时序连贯的中间数据表。\n4. 汇总全量帧的校验后数据，按指定格式封装每帧的位置框、类别与置信度明细，附加关键指标统计说明，生成可追溯的任务交付清单供下游调用。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 我将在此视频监控场景下检测这段视频里的行人、轿车、公交车和卡车，并输出每帧的位置框、类别和置信度。；参数：{'视频对象': '这段视频', '监控目标': '行人、轿车、公交车和卡车', '输出形式': '每帧的位置框、类别和置信度'}\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '这段视频', '监控目标': '行人、轿车、公交车和卡车', '输出形式': '每帧的位置框、类别和置信度'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"d1cf59ba-9b44-4e2e-92e4-f25fc78da425"},{"content":"我将使用视频对象分析工具来检测您上传视频中的行人、轿车、公交车和卡车。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":257,"prompt_tokens":13301,"total_tokens":13558,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":108,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":257},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13301}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-27c520fc-b631-954c-8353-9c8fb54ea5c5","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9ddd-ade2-7a62-ae3c-ffd6d8ac438c-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"video_object_analytics","args":{"camera_id":"CAM_TRAFFIC_001","capture_seconds":2,"interval_seconds":1,"labels":"[\"person\", \"car\", \"bus\", \"truck\"]","operation":"detect","video_path":"/mnt/user-data/uploads/Trafic.mp4"},"id":"call_b27701c9c34748a68f7f5217","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13301,"output_tokens":257,"total_tokens":13558,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":108}}},{"content":"{\"skill\": \"video-object-analytics\", \"status\": \"success\", \"operation\": \"detect\", \"executed_skills\": [\"video-object-analytics\", \"frame-sampling\", \"object-detection\"], \"model\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/models/yolov8n.pt\", \"artifacts\": {\"frames_json\": \"/mnt/user-data/workspace/video-object-analytics/4fba864c090c/frames.json\", \"detections_json\": \"/mnt/user-data/workspace/video-object-analytics/4fba864c090c/detections.json\"}, \"summary\": {\"frame_count\": 3, \"per_frame\": [{\"frame_id\": \"CAM_TRAFFIC_001_202605201000000800_0001\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-20T10:00:00+08:00\", \"counts\": {\"bus\": 2, \"car\": 9}, \"object_count\": 11}, {\"frame_id\": \"CAM_TRAFFIC_001_202605201000010800_0002\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-20T10:00:01+08:00\", \"counts\": {\"bus\": 2, \"car\": 9}, \"object_count\": 11}, {\"frame_id\": \"CAM_TRAFFIC_001_202605201000020800_0003\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-20T10:00:02+08:00\", \"counts\": {\"bus\": 1, \"car\": 9}, \"object_count\": 10}], \"frame_detection_totals\": {\"bus\": 5, \"car\": 27}, \"total_frame_detections\": 32, \"unique_object_count\": null, \"unique_object_count_note\": \"Detection frames are not deduplicated; use operation=track for cross-frame identities.\", \"model\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/models/yolov8n.pt\"}}","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"video_object_analytics","id":"88df766c-870e-4a9a-bdeb-dbf9e05975c7","tool_call_id":"call_b27701c9c34748a68f7f5217","artifact":null,"status":"success"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":85,"prompt_tokens":13943,"total_tokens":14028,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":18,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":85},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13943}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-1bc8f6bc-beef-998b-911d-e25b39c5d209","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f9dde-02c2-7f11-9696-5c78a6e0ceac-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"description":"读取逐帧检测结果详情","path":"/mnt/user-data/workspace/video-object-analytics/4fba864c090c/detections.json"},"id":"call_9da48d2850e4436cbc063608","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13943,"output_tokens":85,"total_tokens":14028,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":18}}},{"content":"{\n  \"skill\": \"object-detection\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.5796,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"detections\": [\n      {\n        \"frame_id\": \"CAM_TRAFFIC_001_202605201000000800_0001\",\n        \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-20T10:00:00+08:00\",\n        \"objects\": [\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_001\",\n            \"label\": \"bus\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.8372,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              572.65,\n              178.51,\n              675.0,\n              318.94\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"bus\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_002\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.6346,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              421.48,\n              348.23,\n              522.5,\n              443.23\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_003\",\n            \"label\": \"bus\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5573,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              426.48,\n              102.59,\n              471.02,\n              159.81\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"bus\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_004\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5432,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              484.47,\n              168.8,\n              528.33,\n              208.64\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_005\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5426,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              29.59,\n              193.45,\n              98.04,\n              239.1\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_006\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5177,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              203.29,\n              160.09,\n              253.03,\n              192.85\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_007\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5052,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              715.58,\n              161.73,\n              779.93,\n              194.68\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_008\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.4766,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              379.88,\n              217.86,\n              447.83,\n              269.97\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_009\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.4444,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              773.71,\n              171.49,\n              804.52,\n              195.68\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_010\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.3839,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              97.93,\n              194.64,\n              154.26,\n              246.22\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0001_011\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.366,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              1163.93,\n              205.42,\n              1279.08,\n              245.26\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"frame_id\": \"CAM_TRAFFIC_001_202605201000010800_0002\",\n        \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-20T10:00:01+08:00\",\n        \"objects\": [\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_001\",\n            \"label\": \"bus\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.8416,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              572.2,\n              152.84,\n              652.45,\n              270.43\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"bus\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_002\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.813,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              376.96,\n              468.77,\n              514.39,\n              605.85\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_003\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.7756,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              447.39,\n              273.41,\n              527.35,\n              347.73\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_004\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.7317,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              157.89,\n              178.36,\n              219.19,\n              221.19\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_005\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.6794,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              20.3,\n              230.07,\n              96.99,\n              288.62\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_006\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5893,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              488.93,\n              149.29,\n              528.83,\n              177.71\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_007\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5195,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              421.36,\n              182.37,\n              476.34,\n              227.75\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_008\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.4879,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              100.63,\n              173.43,\n              148.34,\n              207.07\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_009\",\n            \"label\": \"bus\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.4864,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              23.25,\n              132.6,\n              100.95,\n              204.32\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"bus\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_010\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.423,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              1164.76,\n              205.9,\n              1279.1,\n              246.11\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0002_011\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.4099,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              534.81,\n              114.88,\n              582.28,\n              164.66\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"frame_id\": \"CAM_TRAFFIC_001_202605201000020800_0003\",\n        \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-20T10:00:02+08:00\",\n        \"objects\": [\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0003_001\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.8301,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              468.51,\n              227.36,\n              530.95,\n              280.05\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0003_002\",\n            \"label\": \"bus\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.8039,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              575.26,\n              139.02,\n              643.5,\n              236.52\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"bus\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0003_003\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.7745,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              425.17,\n              350.9,\n              519.73,\n              442.75\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0003_004\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5964,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              22.91,\n              197.97,\n              92.08,\n              240.83\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0003_005\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5668,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              94.33,\n              197.16,\n              170.98,\n              251.04\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0003_006\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5411,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              642.46,\n              148.25,\n              677.17,\n              173.39\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0003_007\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5079,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              451.57,\n              159.67,\n              495.42,\n              194.42\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0003_008\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.5007,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              94.61,\n              209.94,\n              149.35,\n              250.35\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0003_009\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.497,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              175.65,\n              168.91,\n              226.68,\n              209.11\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"object_id\": \"det_0003_010\",\n            \"label\": \"car\",\n            \"confidence\": 0.3638,\n            \"bbox\": [\n              1162.97,\n              205.52,\n              1279.09,\n              247.37\n            ],\n            \"model_label\": \"car\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"model\": \"/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/models/yolov8n.pt\"\n  }\n}\n","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"tool","name":"read_file","id":"68253495-9817-4038-ba29-c46e9d3a92eb","tool_call_id":"call_9da48d2850e4436cbc063608","artifact":null,"status":"success"}],"viewed_images":{},"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/3994872d-9d99-4674-bf36-2891014663a1/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/3994872d-9d99-4674-bf36-2891014663a1/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/3994872d-9d99-4674-bf36-2891014663a1/user-data/outputs"},"uploaded_files":[{"filename":"Trafic.mp4","size":75965424,"path":"/mnt/user-data/uploads/Trafic.mp4","extension":".mp4"}],"title":"Traffic Video Object Detection","raw_messages":[{"content":"<uploaded_files>\nThe following files were uploaded in this message:\n\n- Trafic.mp4 (72.4 MB)\n  Path: /mnt/user-data/uploads/Trafic.mp4\n\nYou can read these files using the `read_file` tool with the paths shown above.\n</uploaded_files>\n\n检测这段视频里的行人、轿车、公交车和卡车，输出每帧的位置框、类别和置信度。","additional_kwargs":{"files":[{"filename":"Trafic.mp4","size":75965424,"path":"/mnt/user-data/uploads/Trafic.mp4","status":"uploaded"}]},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"b5d1e8e5-9c98-4b90-8c17-19be4e0696d1"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze-video</name>\n      <description>专业视频抽帧与取证准备技能。支持场景检测、多阶段帧提取和 metadata 生成，供 single-video-event-analysis 做 LLM 审帧使用；本 skill 不再作为最终事件检测入口。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/analyze-video/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>batch-video-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Batch ingest local monitoring videos into the Elasticsearch video library after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, with metadata, sampled-frame object summaries, and searchable documents. For direct user video ingestion, ingest-and-embed, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, or business video-library requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear ingestion plan, video directory, video manifest, camera_id, or multiple video files to index for later retrieval and statistics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/batch-video-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>camera-health-check</name>\n      <description>Check video monitoring camera quality from sampled frames and return health status before downstream event generation. Use when Codex has camera_id and frames and needs to gate or downgrade event confidence for offline, unavailable, degraded, black-screen, blurred, occluded, frozen, corrupted, or shifted camera feeds.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/camera-health-check/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>city-video-intelligence</name>\n      <description>Business orchestration for city video intelligence requests. Use when users ask for monitoring video search, semantic video retrieval, event review, object statistics, evidence packages, video ingestion, camera health operations, cross-camera analysis, or role-based scenarios such as traffic police, property security, urban management, emergency management, or legal evidence preparation. Also use it when the user asks what the current data and skills can or cannot support (capability-boundary questions) — it answers with an explicit capability_gap instead of guessing. This skill maps business intent to existing custom video skills and prevents ad hoc code generation unless the user explicitly asks for development or testing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/city-video-intelligence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>duplicate-event-merge</name>\n      <description>Merge duplicate video event candidates from the same camera, event type, ROI, evidence frames, or overlapping time window. Use after single-video-event-analysis or batch video analysis when Codex has a list of Event Candidate records and needs canonical events plus duplicate mappings.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/duplicate-event-merge/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-package-generation</name>\n      <description>Generate an evidence package manifest for indexed monitoring videos or event/search results, including snapshot evidence and optional short video clips. Use when Codex needs a package_id, manifest URI, evidence items, hashes, and reusable evidence artifacts.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-package-generation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>evidence-snapshot</name>\n      <description>Generate snapshot evidence for video monitoring event candidates. Use when Codex has an event, event_id, evidence_frame_ids, image_uri, or frame list and needs a snapshot URI, SHA-256 integrity hash, created_at timestamp, privacy masking status, and Evidence schema output.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/evidence-snapshot/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>ffmpeg-utils</name>\n      <description>视频处理工具集，支持视频截取和关键帧提取。常用于将监控视频剪辑为证据片段。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/ffmpeg-utils/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>frame-sampling</name>\n      <description>Sample structured frames from an existing video file. Use when Codex has video_path, file_path, raw_segment_uri, camera_id, sampling_strategy, capture_seconds, or provided frame records and needs stable Frame schema outputs. This skill exposes OpenCV-backed real video frame extraction.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/frame-sampling/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>human-review-routing</name>\n      <description>Decide whether video monitoring event candidates require manual review. Use after event generation and evidence creation when Codex has event confidence, event_type, review_threshold, camera_health, high_risk_event_types, newly added camera signals, or enforcement-impact flags and needs review queue routing.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/human-review-routing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-detection</name>\n      <description>Detect visible objects in sampled video frames and return standard Detection schema only. Use when Codex needs YOLO labels, confidences, and bounding boxes for people, vehicles, or COCO objects. Do not use this skill to infer events, abnormal behavior, accidents, fights, falls, congestion, intrusion, smoke/fire, or business semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-detection/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-statistics</name>\n      <description>Compute object statistics for monitoring videos from Elasticsearch video-library records or local detections/tracks JSON. Use when Codex needs counts by label, camera, time bucket, or movement state.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-statistics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>object-tracking</name>\n      <description>Track detected objects across video frames and return Track schema for object analytics only. Use when Codex has frame-level detections and needs stable track ids, trajectories, duration, last bbox, movement state, confidence, and evidence frame ids. Do not use this skill to infer video events or abnormal behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/object-tracking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>privacy-masking</name>\n      <description>Mask sensitive visual data in video evidence such as faces, license plates, phone numbers, and doorplates. Use when Codex has an evidence image URI and explicit sensitive_regions bbox coordinates, or privacy_masking config and needs a masked URI before exposing snapshots or clips externally. This skill exposes OpenCV image read/write and Gaussian blur masking for real files.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/privacy-masking/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>roi-mapping</name>\n      <description>Match detections or tracks against configured camera ROI polygons for geometric object analytics. Use when Codex has camera_id plus tracks or objects and needs point containment or bbox overlap matches for configured areas. Do not use this skill to decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/roi-mapping/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>single-video-event-analysis</name>\n      <description>Analyze one local monitoring video for incidents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request, by extracting timestamped frames and having the LLM review visible evidence. Use for fight, fall, traffic accident, congestion, crowd gathering, smoke/fire, intrusion, illegal occupation, or other abnormal events. For direct user monitoring-video event questions, load city-video-intelligence first. This skill is the only custom event-detection entrypoint; YOLO/object detection may be used only as optional object context and must not decide event semantics.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/single-video-event-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-embedding-index</name>\n      <description>Generate text embeddings or StreetModel sampled-frame image embeddings for video-library documents after city-video-intelligence has routed the request. Only enrich citybrain-video-library in place. For direct user StreetModel, ingest-and-embed, semantic retrieval, benchmark, or keyword-vs-vector requests, load city-video-intelligence first.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-embedding-index/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-object-analytics</name>\n      <description>Deterministic structured entrypoint for local-video object detection and cross-frame tracking. Use for direct requests to count visible people, vehicles, or other objects, or to track them across frames. The dedicated video_object_analytics tool owns all CLI parameters, model configuration, persistent paths, and downstream skill order.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-object-analytics/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-search</name>\n      <description>Search indexed monitoring videos from text, images, structured filters, or precomputed vectors. Use for keyword retrieval, LLM-optimized text-to-video semantic retrieval, combined keyword/vector search, or image-to-video similarity search against StreetModel/Qwen3-VL video vectors.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-segment-extraction</name>\n      <description>Extract playable short video evidence clips around event times. Use when Codex has event_id, camera_id, raw_segment_uri, event_time, event_elapsed_seconds, pre_seconds, or post_seconds and needs an MP4 clip URI plus clip time range. This skill exposes FFmpeg-backed clipping for real local videos and memory-backed synthetic clips for tests.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-segment-extraction/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>video-stream-ingestion</name>\n      <description>Normalize an existing local video file after city-video-intelligence has routed a video-library or analysis request, returning raw segment/session metadata such as duration, resolution, frame rate, codec, and session times. Use it for any \"read this video's duration / resolution / fps / codec / metadata\" or \"turn this video into a standard analysis input\" request instead of running ffprobe by hand. For direct user ingestion, Elasticsearch, StreetModel, search, statistics, evidence, or camera-health requests, load city-video-intelligence first. Use this atomic skill when Codex already has a clear plan and a local MP4/MOV/AVI/MKV file before frame sampling.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/video_surveillance/video-stream-ingestion/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"fe6654c5-46eb-4e9c-9d77-3b04a014fc08"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：视频监控。场景ID：video_surveillance\n识别场景：视频监控 (video_surveillance)；场景模式：single；候选场景：video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 检测这段视频里的行人、轿车、公交车和卡车，输出每帧的位置框、类别和置信度。\n任务规划：\n1. 调用视频解析组件读取输入源，完成视频流解码与逐帧抽帧处理，核对分辨率与编码格式以适配后续视觉模型，产出标准化帧序列及基础元数据。\n2. 基于视频监控场景的多目标检测能力，将抽帧序列依次输入识别引擎，针对行人、轿车、公交车和卡车执行推理计算，并应用预设置信度阈值过滤低质量预测，产出逐帧原始检测结果集。\n3. 对原始检测结果进行坐标空间转换与时序逻辑校验，依据连续帧间目标运动规律剔除异常跳变框与重叠冗余框，统一数据输出口径，产出结构化且时序连贯的中间数据表。\n4. 汇总全量帧的校验后数据，按指定格式封装每帧的位置框、类别与置信度明细，附加关键指标统计说明，生成可追溯的任务交付清单供下游调用。\n场景任务：\n- video_surveillance: 我将在此视频监控场景下检测这段视频里的行人、轿车、公交车和卡车，并输出每帧的位置框、类别和置信度。；参数：{'视频对象': '这段视频', '监控目标': '行人、轿车、公交车和卡车', '输出形式': '每帧的位置框、类别和置信度'}\n已提取参数：{'视频对象': '这段视频', '监控目标': '行人、轿车、公交车和卡车', '输出形式': '每帧的位置框、类别和置信度'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：视频对象。需要分析的监控视频、摄像头、视频流、录像文件、实时画面、卡口视频或视频帧\n- 提取可选参数：监控目标。需要识别或分析的对象、行为或事件，如人员聚集、车辆违停、越界、烟火、异常停留、摔倒、入侵、打架、遗留物、通行计数等\n- 提取可选参数：时间范围。视频分析的起止时间、日期、时段、时刻或实时窗口\n- 提取可选参数：输出形式。用户期望的输出，如告警、截图、时间点清单、检测结果、表格、报告、标注说明或风险摘要\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"d1cf59ba-9b44-4e2e-92e4-f25fc78da425"},{"content":"我将使用视频对象分析工具来检测您上传视频中的行人、轿车、公交车和卡车。\n\n","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":257,"prompt_tokens":13301,"total_tokens":13558,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":108,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":257},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13301}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,